8. MASKED DETECTOR REGION IMPLEMENTATION — 2026-11-14

Implemented ssl.mode=regions in mlpf/model/ssl_regions.py and mlpf/model/ssl.py.
The MLPF backbone is unchanged. An auxiliary cross-attention predictor reads
visible-hit embeddings and fixed surface/angular region queries. All hits in
queried regions are removed before student feature engineering. Target-surface
selection is random; angular query selection uses only activity on other,
non-target surfaces. No hidden hit positions, centroids, counts, or energies
are supplied to the predictor. Two independently masked student views are used.

Input-derived targets are supported-cell occupancy, hit count, and measured
calorimeter deposited energy, including empty cells. Optional EMA teacher
prototype targets use mean embeddings of hits within each nonempty region.
Loss weights: occupancy BCE 1, Poisson NLL 0.1, log1p-energy Huber 1, latent CE 0.1.
Detector types and events are balanced. Tracker energy is not a training target.
The old thinning objective remains available; incompatible track/cluster schemas
are rejected by region mode. Standard MLPF exports exclude the auxiliary head.

The fixed catalogue contains 23,617 angular regions from 2,048 training events.
This is empirical support, not a complete detector active-channel map. Regions
are layer-local eta/phi patches, not exact modules or consecutive-depth blocks.
Default query budgets are 128 tracker and 512 calo regions. A 64-event held-out
sampling audit measured mean removal of 9.60% tracker / 19.11% calo, with mean
catalogue target coverage 99.991%. These are measured mask rates, not detector
inefficiency estimates. Query selection invariance to hidden content is tested.

GPU benchmark on the maximum-size event among the full 20,000-event input pool
(14,703 hits), RTX 5060 Ti 16GB, two views, bfloat16:
  Batch 1: 7.54 GiB reserved, 2.663 events/s.
  Batch 2: 14.59 GiB reserved, 2.829 events/s.
Batch 1 is the local default to leave headroom for random mask density; batch 2
offers only 6.2% additional throughput. The recipe uses 100,000 updates to retain
the previous run's 100,000 sampled-event exposure. This does not match optimizer
step count or wall time. No long training run was launched in this implementation.

Validation: 36 tests passed across region SSL, legacy SSL, hit probes,
visualization, and diagnostics. Tests include exact interrupted/resumed training,
strict standard MLPF export, gradients/frozen teacher, periodic phi, padding,
and empty/occupied targets. GPU smoke completed 30 updates and resumed through
31, including PF probes, CPU hit-pair probes, embedding snapshots, and plots.
The combined training_and_probes plot now shows the region objective terms.

Smoke results are pipeline checks only: 64 training / 4 validation events,
10-update PF probes. At step 30, validation occupancy BCE was 0.4074, energy
Huber loss 0.00614, and total loss 1.1323. Occupancy accuracy was 0.8578 but
precision/recall/F1 were all zero at threshold 0.5: the head predicted all cells
empty at that threshold. A constant low occupancy probability can already lower
BCE substantially; declining loss alone is not evidence of useful context.
PF F1 also fell from 0.0863 to zero with these deliberately tiny probe budgets.
Neither result establishes the long-run behavior of the new objective. Longer
training, matched probes, and geometry-only/context-ablation controls are needed.

