9. COMPLETED REGION TRAINING ANALYSIS — 2026-11-15

Run: experiments/cld_hits_ssl_regions. Completed 100,000 updates, batch 1,
20,000-event training pool (100,000 sampled-event exposures). Probes use 1,024
training / 256 validation events and 1,000 readout updates with seed 31415.
SSL validation uses 128 events with fixed masks; two views per event.

PF results (untrained means an initialized encoder with a trained PF readout):
                          Initial    40k       60k       80k       100k
  Matched particle F1     0.34361    0.37721   0.40014   0.40306   0.41620
  Matched PID accuracy    0.67248    0.68512   0.75880   0.76549   0.75403
  Unweighted task loss    2.37238    2.23135   2.00954   2.04818   2.04909
  Event energy rel. MAE   0.22449    0.15501   0.12397   0.09837   0.11026
  Particle count MAE      16.4336    13.1953   17.0234   17.5352   17.3594

Final versus initialized PF F1 improves by 0.0726 (21.1% relative). Most of the
matching improvement is purity (0.3487 -> 0.4603); efficiency improves less
(0.3386 -> 0.3798). Final mean count is 78.52 versus 95.16 targets, a -16.64
bias versus initial -2.75. Matched-particle relative energy error worsens from
0.2067 to 0.2301 even though total-event energy error improves substantially.
MET absolute error improves 21.61 -> 16.68. These metrics measure distinct tasks;
the gain is not uniform across all reconstruction criteria.

Earlier thinning run at equal final exposure (batch 2 x 50k updates): PF F1
0.37457, matched PID 0.68901, event energy rel. MAE 0.13151, task loss 2.38084.
Its best sampled PF F1 was 0.38237 at 80k event exposure. Region masking is
promising by these measures, but this is one SSL/probe seed and changes both
the objective and batch/update count. Initial encoder tensors in saved step-0
probe checkpoints are exactly equal. Stored initial embedding arrays differ
slightly (mean abs difference 0.000913), and trained initial PF results differ
(region F1 0.34361 versus thinning 0.33032). A definitive comparison requires
matched repeated probe fitting; nominally equal seeds do not remove observed
numerical/optimization variability. No causal attribution to augmentation alone.

Region objective: first logged validation (2k) -> final (100k):
  Occupancy BCE 0.37397 -> 0.19330; count NLL 1.28581 -> 0.47568.
  Log1p-energy Huber 0.005032 -> 0.003027.
  Total loss 0.96668 -> 0.29290; latent CE 4.59096 -> 0.49005.
  Occupancy F1 ~0 -> 0.69968; precision 0.76847, recall 0.64495 at final.
  Accuracy 0.92202 versus all-empty baseline 0.85814.
The all-empty behavior observed in the smoke run did not persist. Last-2k mean
train loss 0.29364 is close to validation 0.29290: no obvious aggregate SSL
overfitting, although this is not a generalization guarantee. Mask rates are
9.25% tracker / 18.40% calo, catalogue coverage 99.9929% on 128 validation events.
Energy is only about 1% of the final scalar objective; loss scale alone does not
measure its gradient contribution. Final teacher effective prototypes average
8.21 per event/view out of 256, versus 176.54 at 2k. This narrowing deserves an
ablation; it is not evidence that the full embeddings have collapsed.

NEW INFERENCE-ONLY CONTEXT CHECK:
Checkpoint 100k; first 64 held-out events, two fixed masks each. Kept recipient
queries, geometry, targets, token count and detector composition fixed; replaced
visible student embeddings with those from the next held-out event (cyclic donor,
deterministically resampled within detector type to match token counts).
                          Correct context     Foreign-event context
  Occupancy F1, balanced   0.70283             0.11290
  Tracker occupancy F1    0.56602             0.06097
  Calo occupancy F1       0.77018             0.14113
  Occupancy BCE           0.19168             0.91513
  Count NLL               0.47403             3.40408
  Calo energy Huber       0.003001            0.006160
Zero memory gives F1 0; it is an out-of-distribution control, not a separately
trained geometry-only baseline. The fixed trained region predictor depends on
event-specific memory. This does not isolate backbone contextual reasoning from
auxiliary-head attention, nor rule out simple geometric interpolation/density
estimation, nor establish particle association. No weights were updated.

HIT-PAIR PROBES (oracle foreground, fixed local candidate edges, 256 events):
                     Raw       Init embedding    Final embedding
  Tracker AP         0.38573   0.46401           0.48896
  Tracker ROC AUC    0.70298   0.72622           0.77067
  Calo AP            0.97760   0.94659           0.96330
  Calo ROC AUC       0.85462   0.69069           0.77230
Tracker AP gain over initialized embeddings is +0.02496, event-bootstrap 95%
interval [0.02084, 0.02912]; calo AUC gain is +0.08161 [0.07776, 0.08563].
These intervals condition on fitted models, not SSL/probe seed uncertainty.
Calo pair prevalence is 90.34%; high AP alone is weak evidence. Its final AUC
still trails raw features by 0.08232. The new representation does not yet beat
raw geometry/measurements for this calorimeter association probe.

EMBEDDING EVOLUTION:
Fixed four-event cohort: 8,192 hits, 846 tracker / 7,346 calo. Global CKA to
initialization 0.61594. Centered covariance entropy-effective rank changes
tracker 8.38 -> 6.64, calo 5.74 -> 4.07 (256 embedding dimensions). Feature
scale grows substantially. These are anisotropic embeddings, not constant
embeddings; rank is not a direct measure of PF information. Late cosine-kNN
overlap (90k -> 100k, 15 neighbors, fixed 2,000-hit subset) is 93.2% tracker /
86.5% calo, versus 63.4% / 40.2% initial -> final. Late structure is relatively
stable. The small cohort and cross-event neighbor selection limit interpretation.

PERFORMANCE:
100k training updates total 8.06 hours, mean 3.45 events/s. Logged period from
first training step through final probe/checkpoint is 9.86 hours, excluding the
initial probe. Maximum recorded step allocated GPU memory is 7.15 GiB; this does
not include the initial probe peak. These timings are not GPU utilization samples.

NEXT DECISIVE COMPARISONS:
  1. Longer matched PF probes, several seeds, initial / 60k / 80k / 100k and
     corresponding thinning checkpoints. Choose metric before selecting epoch.
  2. Remove latent loss at matched budgets to test whether teacher distillation
     adds value beyond masked input prediction; do not infer this from CE alone.
  3. Fit geometry-only and simple neighboring-layer interpolation baselines for
     region targets. Test stronger contiguous-depth masks only after this control.
  4. Investigate calo association with raw+embedding probes and per-class PF
     diagnostics; improved occupancy completion is not automatically grouping.

