but no observed late reversal in the region validation F1 curve.

The previous short-probe undercounting concern is substantially reduced with
longer training: region mean count bias is now -5.85 particles/event, versus
-16.64 in the single-seed periodic 1,000-update final probe. This comparison also
changes seed aggregation, so it is not a pure within-seed causal estimate.
Mean region event energy error .141 differs from the earlier .110 single-seed
result; use the matched multi-seed result for the cross-method conclusion.

CONCLUSION AND NEXT STEP:
The masked-region recipe gives a consistent PF advantage over thinning under
this matched five-seed readout evaluation. It is not merely an artifact of a
short readout budget or one favorable probe seed. Evidence remains conditional
on one SSL training seed per method, reused validation events, and equal event
exposure rather than equal optimizer steps or compute. This does not attribute
the gain specifically to masking, measured-content prediction, or latent loss.
Next useful ablation: the same region recipe with latent_weight=0, preserving
data, masks, initialization and event exposure, then the same matched probes.
The new ablation was not launched during this results check.

